    {
      "key": "choice-16-stem",
      "serialized": "Use the polyline [[MATH:0]] shown in the figure. A function assigns each input exactly one output; different inputs may share an output. Correspondence I has every point of [[MATH:1]] as an input and assigns its [[MATH:2]]-coordinate as output. Correspondence II has every real number in [[MATH:3]] as an input and relates it to the points of [[MATH:4]] having that [[MATH:5]]-coordinate. Select every true statement.",
      "lines": [
        "Use the polyline [[MATH:0]] shown in the figure. A function assigns each input exactly one output; different inputs may share an output.",
        "",
        "Correspondence I has every point of [[MATH:1]] as an input and assigns its [[MATH:2]]-coordinate as output.",
        "",
        "Correspondence II has every real number in [[MATH:3]] as an input and relates it to the points of [[MATH:4]] having that [[MATH:5]]-coordinate.",
        "",
        "Select every true statement."
      ],
